# FocusGrid runtime configuration (CONFIGURATION.md CFG-01).
# All variables below are server-only. None affect local task CRUD, and none
# adjust priority weights or quadrant boundaries. Copy to .env.local to change.

FOCUSGRID_AI_MODE=off
FOCUSGRID_DEPLOYMENT=local

# Only used when FOCUSGRID_AI_MODE=provider (local development only).
# FOCUSGRID_AI_PROVIDER=openai
# FOCUSGRID_AI_MODEL=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# V2 assistant + Telegram bot (optional, local deployments only). Any one key
# enables it; the first one found picks the provider. Override with
# FOCUSGRID_LLM_PROVIDER = anthropic | openai | xai | groq | openrouter | ollama | custom,
# FOCUSGRID_LLM_MODEL, FOCUSGRID_LLM_API_KEY, FOCUSGRID_LLM_BASE_URL (custom/self-hosted).
# Anthropic uses native web search; other providers get a built-in server-side search.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# FOCUSGRID_LLM_PROVIDER=
# FOCUSGRID_LLM_MODEL=

# V2 Telegram capture bot (optional; needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). Create a bot with
# @BotFather, then message it once — it replies with your chat id if unlisted.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Voice notes in/out on the bot use OpenAI speech APIs (whisper-1 / gpt-4o-mini-tts)
# with the OPENAI_API_KEY above; without it the bot is text-only.

# V2 push reminders (optional). Generate with: npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# Reminders are scheduled from the browser and delivered by this server even
# when the tab is closed. Unset = the Settings section explains how to enable it.
# FOCUSGRID_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# FOCUSGRID_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# FOCUSGRID_VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com
